# trans-crotonic acid (CH3-CH=CH-COOH, 13C4-labeled, 7-spin NMR system)
# Reference [12]: Knill et al., PRL 86, 5811 (2001)
#
# Nuclei (7):
#   0 = C1  (COOH carboxyl carbon)
#   1 = C2  (=CH- olefinic, bonded to C1)
#   2 = C3  (-CH= olefinic, bonded to C4)
#   3 = C4  (-CH3 methyl carbon)
#   4 = H1  (vinyl H on C2)
#   5 = H2  (vinyl H on C3)
#   6 = M   (methyl protons, 3 equivalent H on C4)
#
# W formula: W(u,v) = round(10000 / (4 * J_Hz))          [two-qubit]
#            W(u,u) = round(pi * 10000 / |delta_shift_Hz|) [single-qubit]
#
# J-coupling values (Hz) from published NMR literature (approximate):
#   1-bond C-C:  J(C1,C2)=41.6  J(C2,C3)=67.7  J(C3,C4)=44.7
#   1-bond C-H:  J(C2,H1)=157   J(C3,H2)=150   J(C4,M)=126
#   3-bond H-H:  J(H1,H2)=16    (trans vinyl)
#   2-3 bond:    J(C1,H1)=7.4   J(C2,H2)=7.0   J(C1,C3)=1.7
#                J(C3,H1)=4.0   J(C1,H2)=3.5   J(C2,C4)=2.6
#   Long range:  J(C1,C4)=0.4   J(C4,H1)=0.75  J(C4,H2)=0.5  (others <0.2)
#
# Units: 1/10000 s (same as acetyl chloride)
7
# --- Single-qubit gate times (from chemical shift separations) ---
single 0 7.0
single 1 36.0
single 2 36.0
single 3 2.0
single 4 57.0
single 5 57.0
single 6 15.0
# --- Fast two-qubit interactions (W <= 100, direct bonds) ---
two 1 2 37.0
two 2 3 56.0
two 0 1 60.0
two 3 6 20.0
two 2 5 17.0
two 1 4 16.0
# --- Medium interactions (100 < W <= 1000, 2-3 bond couplings) ---
two 4 5 156.0
two 0 4 338.0
two 1 5 357.0
two 2 4 625.0
two 0 5 714.0
two 1 3 962.0
# --- Slow interactions (W > 1000, long-range) ---
two 0 2 1471.0
two 0 3 6250.0
two 3 4 3333.0
two 3 5 5000.0
two 0 6 9999.0
two 1 6 9999.0
two 2 6 9999.0
two 4 6 9999.0
two 5 6 9999.0
